==Strategy==
You should have ALL [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] before attempting this stage. If not, Alpacky will kill your [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] in four or less hits, but you want him to survive FIVE hits or you may not be able to beat this stage.

Assuming sufficient [[Treasure]]s, this level is very simple with quick attackers. Take cheap and fast cats: [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] are good candidates. Spam Lions immediately as you save up for Awakened Bahamut. Then send Manic Erasers and Lions until the enemy base is destroyed. Tackey will shoot over the top of your attackers, and they should be able to destroy the base quickly.

Money starting [[Cat Combo|Combos]] like [[Paranormal Activity (Combo)|Paranormal Activity]], [[Duet (Combo)|Duet]], [[Crazy Hearts (Combo)|Crazy Hearts]] and [[Headbanger's Ball (Combo)|Headbanger's Ball]] are extremely helpful here for the startoff, letting you rush the base as quick as possible without interruption from the Tackeys. After having these paired with [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher-class units]] like [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]], [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Giraffe Cat]], [[Li'l Cow Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Lion Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] and more, rushing the base is easily done and the level completed.

